<title>UK: Crude pipeline to Russia's Tuapse still shut.</title>
<headline>Crude pipeline to Russia's Tuapse still shut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A crude pipeline feeding Russia's Black Sea port of Tuapse remained shut on Tuesday after closing late on Sunday, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The pipeline was closed at 2200 GMT on Sunday  for scheduled maintenance which should last for &quot;only a few days&quot;, the source added.</p>
<p>One crude tanker berthed early on Tuesday but had not started to load.</p>
<p>Two gas oil vessels were also alongside with another due to arrive later on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Russia's main crude export terminal at Novorossiisk was open and operating normally as was Ukraine's Odessa and the Baltic port of Ventspils, the source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
